+### Drag screening
+
+In Sunniesnow, one of the judgement settings is whether to enable Lyrica 5 mechanics.
+With Lyrica 5 mechanics, an unjudged `drag` note can screen a touch down from hitting another note.
+This check checks that, the drag screening does not make a note that is hittable without Lyrica 5 mechanics
+become unhittable with Lyrica 5 mechanics.
+
+A violation to this check is a `drag` event at time $t_0$ (seconds) that satisfies both the conditions:
+(1) there is no other note (`tap`, `hold`, `drag`, `flick`)
+that is both within spatial distance $L$ from the `drag` event
+and is at a time (seconds) between (inclusive) $t_0-T$ and $t_0$;
+(2) there is some other non-`drag` note (`tap`, `hold`, `flick`)
+that is both within spatial distance $L$ from the `drag` event
+and is at a time (seconds) between (inclusive) $t_0$ and $t_0+T$.
+Here, the screening time $T$ and the screening distance $L$ are parameters of this check,
+whose default values are respectively 0.4 and 40.
+
+When a violation is clicked, the violating `drag` event is selected.
+
